WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.581 --> 00:00:01.414
(exciting fast music)

00:00:01.414 --> 00:00:02.350
- Oh, what's up?

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.350
Hey, Andrew!

00:00:04.691 --> 00:00:06.349
How's it going?

00:00:06.349 --> 00:00:09.230
No come on, let's go, I got
another food adventure for us.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.560
- What are we eating?

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.393
- Pasta.

00:00:12.464 --> 00:00:13.297
- All right.

00:00:13.297 --> 00:00:14.658
- Yeah, that's right.
(fun rhythmic music)

00:00:14.658 --> 00:00:16.474
This guy right here, that's my boy.

00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:17.553
Woo hoo, let's go!

00:00:17.553 --> 00:00:19.704
- This is wet, now I'm wet.

00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:20.782
- Pasta baby.

00:00:20.782 --> 00:00:23.309
We are on our way to eat
three of the best pastas

00:00:23.309 --> 00:00:26.023
in Los Angeles at three
drastically different price points,

00:00:26.023 --> 00:00:28.383
to find out which one is the
most worth it at its price.

00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:29.216
- Worth it.

00:00:29.216 --> 00:00:30.049
- The last stop we're going to,

00:00:30.049 --> 00:00:31.300
I don't know if you're ready for it.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.211
- I've had $300 steak, $130 pizza,

00:00:34.211 --> 00:00:35.572
I think I'm ready for pasta.

00:00:35.572 --> 00:00:37.911
I have a feeling I know what
the highest one is gonna be.

00:00:37.911 --> 00:00:39.260
- No you don't, you ain't ready.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.093
You weren't born ready.

00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:41.820
- Is it truffle though?

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:42.790
- Don't worry about it, man.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.630
We're on our way right
now to Pasta Sister.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:45.463
Can I go this way?

00:00:45.463 --> 00:00:46.774
- No!
- No, no!

00:00:46.774 --> 00:00:48.940
- Do not enter!
- Yes, I can.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:49.773
Where?

00:00:49.773 --> 00:00:50.893
- Oh yeah, it's a one way,
you can go down there.

00:00:50.893 --> 00:00:51.872
- Dang it guys.

00:00:51.872 --> 00:00:55.121
- If you start seeing cars
come towards us, just stop.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:59.473
(serene lighthearted music)

00:00:59.473 --> 00:01:01.581
- I'm Francesco, I'm owner of Pasta Sister

00:01:01.581 --> 00:01:03.068
with my mother, Paola.

00:01:03.068 --> 00:01:05.939
We decided to open this
place because we thought,

00:01:05.939 --> 00:01:08.002
in Los Angeles, there
are many great places,

00:01:08.002 --> 00:01:09.780
but very little made fresh pasta,

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.349
low prices, like we do.

00:01:11.349 --> 00:01:14.240
We start early in the
morning making the pasta.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.142
We make it with Italian flour,

00:01:15.142 --> 00:01:17.409
because not all the
flours make good pasta.

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:19.377
And not all the flour makes it yellow

00:01:19.377 --> 00:01:21.749
and beautiful to stay for seven days,

00:01:21.749 --> 00:01:23.148
like our pasta does.

00:01:23.148 --> 00:01:24.495
- You guys are not sisters, obviously.

00:01:24.495 --> 00:01:25.528
I don't see any sisters here.

00:01:25.528 --> 00:01:27.709
- Sometimes though, they
say I'm the prettiest one.

00:01:27.709 --> 00:01:28.639
(people laughing)

00:01:28.639 --> 00:01:30.970
But my mom and her sister work here.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.999
My sister Georgia, she
works in the front with us.

00:01:32.999 --> 00:01:36.019
Today we're gonna prepare
for you the tagliatelle

00:01:36.019 --> 00:01:38.567
arriabata, our lightly spicy tomato sauce.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:41.305
Put olive oil, chili
flakes, some garlic oil,

00:01:41.305 --> 00:01:43.536
when the pasta is ready,
you put the tomato sauce

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.206
and put the parsleys, the last ingredient.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.446
And the pasta is done.

00:01:47.446 --> 00:01:48.279
(exciting rhythmic music)

00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:49.806
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:01:49.806 --> 00:01:51.765
- Wow, this tastes like the
adult version of root beer.

00:01:51.765 --> 00:01:53.396
Are we gonna eat off the same plate?

00:01:53.396 --> 00:01:54.836
- We got a lot of pasta to eat today,

00:01:54.836 --> 00:01:57.894
let's just avoid any Lady in
the Tramp type situations.

00:01:57.894 --> 00:01:59.074
- Here.

00:01:59.074 --> 00:02:00.907
- Great, I hated that.

00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:04.864
It's very good pasta.

00:02:04.864 --> 00:02:05.697
- That was intense.

00:02:05.697 --> 00:02:08.042
- Every noodle is just blanketed in sauce.

00:02:08.042 --> 00:02:09.061
- I also get that sense that I'm in

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:11.644
his mamas kitchen in Italy.

00:02:11.644 --> 00:02:12.704
I've never been to Italy before but...

00:02:12.704 --> 00:02:13.537
(man laughing)

00:02:13.537 --> 00:02:15.424
- We are gonna prepare, also, gnocchi,

00:02:15.424 --> 00:02:17.194
with a porcini mushroom and cream sauce.

00:02:17.194 --> 00:02:18.935
We use the porcini that
we made in the morning,

00:02:18.935 --> 00:02:20.146
adding some cream.

00:02:20.146 --> 00:02:21.346
Everything made from scratch.

00:02:21.346 --> 00:02:23.838
- [Steven] Fresh gnocchi, he
described this as pillows.

00:02:23.838 --> 00:02:25.626
- [Andrew] Everything that
has ever been described

00:02:25.626 --> 00:02:26.966
as a pillow has been great.

00:02:26.966 --> 00:02:30.377
- This is like the ultimate
pillow fight for my mouth.

00:02:30.377 --> 00:02:31.886
Holy smother.
- That's insane.

00:02:31.886 --> 00:02:33.719
- So is gnocchi pasta?

00:02:38.451 --> 00:02:42.618
- These are easily the
best gnocchi I've ever had.

00:02:44.308 --> 00:02:45.869
Oh man, we haven't had
any of this bread yet.

00:02:45.869 --> 00:02:48.387
- Look how easy it is to
pull apart, no effort at all.

00:02:48.387 --> 00:02:49.889
- It's like mamas best.

00:02:49.889 --> 00:02:52.306
- These are all my moms best recipes.

00:02:52.306 --> 00:02:56.125
But from our secret menu, we
have the spaghetti bottarga,

00:02:56.125 --> 00:02:58.634
with the dry fish eggs from (mumbles).

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.504
- [Steven] We're gonna
definitely get that, yeah buddy.

00:03:00.504 --> 00:03:01.373
- [Andrew] Yeah.

00:03:01.373 --> 00:03:02.254
- You know when you've been a good boy,

00:03:02.254 --> 00:03:05.909
and your mom just gives
you an extra treat.

00:03:05.909 --> 00:03:07.291
Mmm.

00:03:07.291 --> 00:03:08.422
- I mean this flavor is insane,

00:03:08.422 --> 00:03:10.141
it tastes like it's covered in cheese,

00:03:10.141 --> 00:03:11.180
that's how rich it is.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:14.513
- Why is this on the secret menu though?

00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:19.590
My stomach is full but
my heart is (mumbles).

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.873
- I'm not gonna say
anything, so let's just go.

00:03:22.873 --> 00:03:25.372
- Talk about them sisters
though, I mean, not in that way.

00:03:25.372 --> 00:03:27.003
(men laughing)

00:03:27.003 --> 00:03:29.702
- It's like a neighborhood
deli that also makes

00:03:29.702 --> 00:03:31.602
the best pasta you've ever had.

00:03:31.602 --> 00:03:33.782
- They are unapologetic
about being themselves.

00:03:33.782 --> 00:03:35.252
- And they don't even have a bathroom.

00:03:35.252 --> 00:03:37.792
Speaking of which, we gotta
get to the next place ASAP.

00:03:37.792 --> 00:03:38.961
- Pasta fact!

00:03:38.961 --> 00:03:41.044
- Pasta fact, pasta fact!

00:03:42.963 --> 00:03:44.242
(man screaming)

00:03:44.242 --> 00:03:46.903
- According to the International
Pasta Organization,

00:03:46.903 --> 00:03:48.444
how many different shapes of pasta

00:03:48.444 --> 00:03:49.724
are produced throughout the world?

00:03:49.724 --> 00:03:51.751
- There's an International
Pasta Organization?

00:03:51.751 --> 00:03:52.584
100.

00:03:52.584 --> 00:03:53.417
(man loud screaming)

00:03:53.417 --> 00:03:54.250
600?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.764
- Whoa!

00:03:55.764 --> 00:03:56.597
Did you cheat?

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:57.520
You cheated.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.353
- No, I didn't.

00:03:58.353 --> 00:03:59.840
- There's more than 600 kinds, yes.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.051
- Really?
- Wowza!

00:04:01.051 --> 00:04:03.732
So right now we're on
our way Osteria Mamma.

00:04:03.732 --> 00:04:05.871
How do you say excuse me in Italian?

00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:06.704
- Scusa.

00:04:06.704 --> 00:04:07.537
- No it's not.

00:04:07.537 --> 00:04:08.370
- Yeah it is.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.263
- Really?

00:04:09.263 --> 00:04:11.201
- Scusa, scusa papa pasta.

00:04:11.201 --> 00:04:12.034
- There you go.

00:04:12.034 --> 00:04:15.284
- Do I sound remotely, at all, correct?

00:04:16.433 --> 00:04:19.823
(exciting fun music)

00:04:19.823 --> 00:04:22.802
- This is Osteria Mamma,
my name is Filippo Cortivo.

00:04:22.802 --> 00:04:23.635
I am the owner.

00:04:23.635 --> 00:04:25.391
We opened this restaurant,
a gift to my mother.

00:04:25.391 --> 00:04:27.170
That's why mamma is the name.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:28.352
This is our home.

00:04:28.352 --> 00:04:30.151
The dough, we have flour from Italy,

00:04:30.151 --> 00:04:32.380
some very delicate double zero flour.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.189
You can't be too fast,
you can't be too slow.

00:04:34.189 --> 00:04:35.503
- [Steven] And that's why
it has to be handmade.

00:04:35.503 --> 00:04:37.021
- [Filippo] That's why we
do everything handmade,

00:04:37.021 --> 00:04:39.288
because we like to keep
control of that process.

00:04:39.288 --> 00:04:41.887
Then we let the pasta dry for
a while, and then it's ready.

00:04:41.887 --> 00:04:43.057
- What are you gonna be serving us today?

00:04:43.057 --> 00:04:44.799
- Today, we'll try two pasta.

00:04:44.799 --> 00:04:46.079
The first dish we're gonna prepare

00:04:46.079 --> 00:04:49.208
is the black squid ink bigoli,
with the bottarga shrimp.

00:04:49.208 --> 00:04:52.218
But first we add cherry
tomato, we shave the bottarga,

00:04:52.218 --> 00:04:53.945
and as always, white wine.

00:04:53.945 --> 00:04:55.927
- What makes really good pasta for you?

00:04:55.927 --> 00:04:58.487
- Perfect pasta for
me, is when the noodles

00:04:58.487 --> 00:04:59.907
combine with the sauce,

00:04:59.907 --> 00:05:01.976
that's the flavor you have
exposed in your mouth.

00:05:01.976 --> 00:05:03.947
- Round two, course one.

00:05:03.947 --> 00:05:06.876
Bigoli neri alla bottarga.

00:05:06.876 --> 00:05:08.077
- I do have a second stomach,

00:05:08.077 --> 00:05:09.888
I just like move it in
place when I need it.

00:05:09.888 --> 00:05:13.557
- I always have my second stomach engaged.

00:05:13.557 --> 00:05:17.927
(light serene music)
- Cheers.

00:05:17.927 --> 00:05:18.938
(man groaning)

00:05:18.938 --> 00:05:20.047
- This is really special.

00:05:20.047 --> 00:05:22.897
- It is true what he said,
the noodles sucked in

00:05:22.897 --> 00:05:24.288
all the flavoring here.

00:05:24.288 --> 00:05:25.797
- This is a flavor explosion.

00:05:25.797 --> 00:05:26.787
- And then when it's in your mouth.

00:05:26.787 --> 00:05:29.870
(loud breath of air)

00:05:32.547 --> 00:05:34.357
- The second dish for you guys is gonna be

00:05:34.357 --> 00:05:37.388
the green spinach pappardelle
in a duck ragu sauce.

00:05:37.388 --> 00:05:39.765
It's extra virgin olive
oil, a little bit of garlic,

00:05:39.765 --> 00:05:41.416
the ground duck all ready pre-cooked,

00:05:41.416 --> 00:05:43.196
so you add a little bit of cherry tomato.

00:05:43.196 --> 00:05:44.029
- [Steven] White wine?

00:05:44.029 --> 00:05:44.862
- [Filippo] You know, we're Italian,

00:05:44.862 --> 00:05:46.095
so we like to put wine everywhere.

00:05:46.095 --> 00:05:46.928
(men laughing)

00:05:46.928 --> 00:05:49.683
What we try to give is like
a little jump in Italy.

00:05:49.683 --> 00:05:51.883
I told before about
explosion in your mouth,

00:05:51.883 --> 00:05:53.292
and the wine is a part of it.

00:05:53.292 --> 00:05:54.553
- It reminds me of me and Andrew,

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.011
we're two very imperfect people,

00:05:56.011 --> 00:06:00.362
but together, perfect
explosion in the world.

00:06:00.362 --> 00:06:01.200
- [Andrew] Sure.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.089
- How's that wine?

00:06:02.089 --> 00:06:02.937
- Luxurious.

00:06:02.937 --> 00:06:05.772
- Mmm, that has a deep smell.

00:06:05.772 --> 00:06:06.881
- How deep does it smell?

00:06:06.881 --> 00:06:08.130
- Kind of like your deep voice.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.031
- Let me get that pasta.

00:06:09.031 --> 00:06:09.864
- Cheers.

00:06:11.211 --> 00:06:12.044
- Yeah.

00:06:13.559 --> 00:06:14.409
- That's a lot of flavor.

00:06:14.409 --> 00:06:15.991
- Control it to your mouth, please.

00:06:15.991 --> 00:06:17.368
- Uncontainable, you know what--

00:06:17.368 --> 00:06:18.201
- Flavor explosion.

00:06:18.201 --> 00:06:19.530
- No, it's not even an explosion anymore,

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.609
it's like dynamite.

00:06:20.609 --> 00:06:21.791
- That is an explosion.

00:06:21.791 --> 00:06:23.570
(loud slurping)

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.549
It's the first time I've
made that sucking noise

00:06:25.549 --> 00:06:26.522
on the show today.

00:06:26.522 --> 00:06:28.397
- This pasta is not just more expensive.

00:06:28.397 --> 00:06:29.819
- You're getting more
there, you're getting that

00:06:29.819 --> 00:06:32.431
meat sauce, you're getting
that complete fish dish.

00:06:32.431 --> 00:06:33.537
- And it's still simple.

00:06:33.537 --> 00:06:35.561
If one of us is pasta,
and one of us is sauce.

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:36.860
Who's pasta, who's sauce?

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:38.773
- Say who you think you are on three.

00:06:38.773 --> 00:06:40.660
One, two, three.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:41.699
- [Both] Pasta.

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:44.949
(men laughing lightly)

00:06:46.349 --> 00:06:47.766
Do you like that?

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:51.498
The squid ink pasta, never
had a noodle like that.

00:06:51.498 --> 00:06:54.630
It was very imperfect and craggly,

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.180
but it was also a thick strand.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:58.998
- I think the best dish we had so far,

00:06:58.998 --> 00:07:00.147
was the duck ragu one.

00:07:00.147 --> 00:07:01.938
- [Adam] Pasta fact, some
of the earliest recorded

00:07:01.938 --> 00:07:03.999
reports of eating noodles come from China

00:07:03.999 --> 00:07:05.666
as early as 5000 BC.

00:07:07.557 --> 00:07:08.799
Pasta fact.

00:07:08.799 --> 00:07:12.300
- All righty, the last
place, the final spot.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:13.987
We're gonna get some truffle pasta.

00:07:13.987 --> 00:07:15.146
- I called it.

00:07:15.146 --> 00:07:17.019
- But this is gonna be different.

00:07:17.019 --> 00:07:20.880
They're gonna be lighting a
wheel of Parmesan on fire.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:22.070
It's dinner and a show.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:24.519
As far as (mumbles), I
freaking love white truffle.

00:07:24.519 --> 00:07:26.352
- Do your pasta dance.

00:07:27.798 --> 00:07:28.881
Cut that out.

00:07:31.107 --> 00:07:32.138
- Pasta.

00:07:32.138 --> 00:07:35.555
(intense dramatic music)

00:07:52.612 --> 00:07:54.581
- What sort of noodle
are you making there?

00:07:54.581 --> 00:07:56.581
And do you make it here?

00:07:57.981 --> 00:07:58.919
(men laughing)

00:07:58.919 --> 00:08:00.069
- So it's an Italian dish,

00:08:00.069 --> 00:08:04.129
but you're putting a French spin on it.

00:08:04.129 --> 00:08:04.962
- Excited.

00:08:04.962 --> 00:08:06.696
Ready for a show.

00:08:06.696 --> 00:08:07.613
- Let's go.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:14.857
That is the white truffle,
you all ready started--

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:36.873
Here you go Andrew.

00:08:48.196 --> 00:08:49.092
Thank you so much Chef.

00:08:49.092 --> 00:08:51.383
But to end the day, we have the $100

00:08:51.383 --> 00:08:54.541
flambeed white truffle pasta dish.

00:08:54.541 --> 00:08:55.374
Are you prepared?

00:08:55.374 --> 00:08:56.950
- I've had five pastas today,

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.269
I think I'm as prepared as I'll ever be.

00:08:59.269 --> 00:09:01.823
So this is the first
time that some theatrics

00:09:01.823 --> 00:09:04.003
have been added to our dining experience.

00:09:04.003 --> 00:09:05.663
Are you gonna have any wine?

00:09:05.663 --> 00:09:06.673
- I'm gonna have a taste.

00:09:06.673 --> 00:09:09.970
(serene light music)

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:10.803
This is splendid.

00:09:10.803 --> 00:09:13.032
I need a moment to
prepare myself to eat it.

00:09:13.032 --> 00:09:14.324
So if you wanna take a bite first,

00:09:14.324 --> 00:09:16.245
I derive pleasure from
watching people eat.

00:09:16.245 --> 00:09:20.245
- I don't like that you're
just watching me eat.

00:09:28.465 --> 00:09:30.105
Damn it.

00:09:30.105 --> 00:09:31.065
You better get in here.

00:09:31.065 --> 00:09:35.232
- I feel like camera guy should
have some before I should.

00:09:38.994 --> 00:09:41.702
- Are you gonna have any of
this because it's really good,

00:09:41.702 --> 00:09:43.092
and I have no self control.

00:09:43.092 --> 00:09:45.592
- Okay, I'm gonna take a bite.

00:09:48.923 --> 00:09:49.756
- How's it going?

00:09:49.756 --> 00:09:50.589
- Mmm.

00:09:50.589 --> 00:09:51.422
- Disappointed?

00:09:51.422 --> 00:09:52.943
- Mmm.

00:09:52.943 --> 00:09:54.460
- [Andrew] No, I don't think so.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.318
- Wow, the white truffle is indescribable.

00:09:57.318 --> 00:10:00.319
And we talked about
flavor explosions today,

00:10:00.319 --> 00:10:04.128
this is the most intense flavor explosion.

00:10:04.128 --> 00:10:07.598
- I just live life one
flavor explosion at a time.

00:10:07.598 --> 00:10:09.486
- You more so do it just
like a bunch at a time,

00:10:09.486 --> 00:10:10.938
you never stop eating.

00:10:10.938 --> 00:10:15.485
You feel like our French
(mumbles) been cemented?

00:10:15.485 --> 00:10:17.055
- I feel like my stomach
has been cemented,

00:10:17.055 --> 00:10:19.343
with about two pounds of pasta.

00:10:19.343 --> 00:10:20.854
- Just admit it.

00:10:20.854 --> 00:10:22.354
- I admit nothing.

00:10:28.576 --> 00:10:32.413
- We just ate six different
pasta dishes in one day.

00:10:32.413 --> 00:10:33.362
You know what's coming?

00:10:33.362 --> 00:10:35.396
Which pasta was the most worth it.

00:10:35.396 --> 00:10:39.224
I do believe that $100 pasta,
it was worth the money.

00:10:39.224 --> 00:10:40.693
You got interact with the chef.

00:10:40.693 --> 00:10:42.202
- The fact that he flambeeded...

00:10:42.202 --> 00:10:43.035
- Yeah.
(quiet burping)

00:10:43.035 --> 00:10:44.641
- Hey, that's a $35 burp right there.

00:10:44.641 --> 00:10:47.113
- But to me, that wasn't the
most worth it, at it's price.

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:50.144
- Osteria Mamma, you
get the handmade pasta,

00:10:50.144 --> 00:10:53.351
married with a great sauce,
no question it's worth it.

00:10:53.351 --> 00:10:55.284
- My worth it winner today, hands down,

00:10:55.284 --> 00:10:57.022
goes to Pasta Sister.
(bell ringing)

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:58.813
- [Andrew] Yeah, I also pick Pasta Sister.

00:10:58.813 --> 00:10:59.772
- Yowza.

00:10:59.772 --> 00:11:03.295
A25 for authentic Italian cuisine straight

00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:06.415
from their handmade pasta to my mouth.

00:11:06.415 --> 00:11:07.703
(man laughing)

00:11:07.703 --> 00:11:08.612
Unbelievable.

00:11:08.612 --> 00:11:12.022
- They had the most incredible
gnocchi I've ever had.

00:11:12.022 --> 00:11:14.771
- I guess we should really
ask Bianci what he thinks,

00:11:14.771 --> 00:11:17.689
considering he is the most
Italian person in this car.

00:11:17.689 --> 00:11:19.610
- He grew up in Ohio.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.693
- Oh, me too.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:22.997
Pasta lavista.

00:11:25.661 --> 00:11:26.494
- No!

00:11:27.731 --> 00:11:29.812
I love it when you call me big pasta.

00:11:29.812 --> 00:11:32.395
(men laughing)

00:11:33.617 --> 00:11:35.111
I just remembered that one.

00:11:35.111 --> 00:11:36.361
- [Man] Oh yes!

